      },
      "message": "zyhybrid: clarify role of rs1 in (Non-CHERI) Address Mode\n\nAs soon as DDC is used as the authorizing capability, the metadata,\nincl. the tag bit, of rs1 becomes irrelevant. Only the address is\nsourced from rs1.\n\nWhile this behavior seems natural, and the specification certainly\ngives that impression, I had to convince myself by looking at CHERI's\nSAIL model [1] that my interpretation of the specification is\ncorrect. Therefore, it seems sensible to spell it out once in prose.\n\n1: https://github.com/CTSRD-CHERI/sail-cheri-riscv/blob/bb07488dac8322fc4a653a01d049e16fa05c9065/src/cheri_addr_checks.sail#L182-L189\n\nSigned-off-by: Florian Schmaus <florian.schmaus@codasip.com>",
